From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: 3D depth for each film

How deep a 3D film sits is a matter of the film and the viewer, and a 3D
TV or projector lets it be moved by shifting one eye's picture sideways.
In frame-sequential 3D the kernel can now do that (fa_depth, see the
common_drivers patch of this series): one eye's picture goes that many
pixels right on its refreshes, provided the video window leaves it the
room on screen.

- CVideoSettings::m_StereoDepth, the playing film's depth in pixels,
  -20 to 20, 0 unless set: positive brings the picture forward, more of
  it out of the screen (the left eye goes right), negative sets it back
  (the right eye goes right).
- It is kept per film in special://profile/stereodepth.json, keyed by the
  film's file as the library knows it, and not in the video database:
  that has no column for it, adding one changes the database's version,
  and the library is often shared by several players. Loaded with the
  film's other video settings, kept when they are stored at stop; a film
  at 0 is dropped from the file. There is no global default: every film
  starts at 0.
- Action stereodepth (992) opens the slider dialog for it, as fs3ddelay
  does for the glasses delay; the picture moves as the slider does.
  Player.StereoDepth shows it ("4 px closer", "4 px further", worded as
  the audio offset's "Ahead by") for a skin button.
- AMLCodec: in frame-sequential 3D the video window is narrowed by the
  depth, so both eyes are scaled to the same narrower width and the one
  the kernel moves stays on screen, and the depth is written to the
  kernel; 0 outside frame-sequential 3D, at the first window of each
  film (a crash may have left it set) and when the decoder closes.
- RendererAML: a depth moved or the eyes swapped while paused (no new
  frame to carry the window) is applied at once, as entering or leaving
  HFR VRR already is, so the picture follows the slider and Invert whether
  the film plays or not.

Shared code: the video setting, its file, the action, the slider and the
info label are generic Kodi; the window and the kernel parameter are
Amlogic only.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
